.TH SERVICE 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
service \- talk to the mitos-services control socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B service
.I subcommand
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A thin client for mitos\-services'
.B /run/mitos\-services/control.sock
-- connects, sends one line, prints whatever it reads back until the
connection closes. Mirrors that daemon's actual protocol rather than a
guessed start/stop/restart\-per\-unit interface it doesn't expose:
.TP
.B status
Request a fresh status summary.
.TP
.B reload
Ask the supervisor to reload its config.
.TP
.B ping
Liveness check; prints
.B PONG
if the daemon is up.
.TP
.B targets
List configured targets and which one is active.
.TP
.BI isolate " target"
Switch to a different target.
.TP
.BI launch " path " "[args...]"
Launch an on\-demand sandboxed app.
.TP
.B apps
List currently launched on\-demand apps.
.TP
.RI [ logs " [" filter "]]"
Print recently buffered log lines, optionally filtered.
.SH NOTES
There is no per\-unit
.BR start / stop / restart :
the daemon itself doesn't have one yet, only whole\-supervisor
.B reload
and whole\-target
.BR isolate .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR, and \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the socket couldn't be reached, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7)
